WEBVTT

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.660
Take this, Shingen!

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.870
Shut up, Kenshin!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.270
They've been at it all day.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.470
Where do they get all that energy?

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.600
Takeda Shingen of Kai,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.910
and Uesugi Kenshin of Echigo.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.390
Even after a full day of battle,

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.970
neither shows any sign of exhaustion.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.260
They've just got way too much energy.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:05.000
598 fights and 598 draws...

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.280
What are these people?

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.970
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.970
<b>Confrontation Maiden</b>

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:57.280
So why are these people fighting again?

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:02.070
It all began with a minor argument 
at a banquet.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.780
An argument?

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.160
From what I heard...

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.330
<i>I'm the strongest!</i>

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.710
<i>No, I am!</i>

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.580
Shingen!                    Kenshin!

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.580
So one picked a fight, 
and the other went along with it?

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.880
And then all this happened?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.010
Does a warrior need an excuse for battle?

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.630
You fight because someone's there to fight.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.390
Shingen, Kenshin...

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.810
I applaud you both!

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.490
Warring States generals

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.950
are such a pain, in their simplicity.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.080
But those two...

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.820
What is it, Hideyoshi?

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.880
U-Um...

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.390
I might be wrong about this, but...

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.220
Say it.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.030
O-OK.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:58.380
Don't you think that maybe 
they're good friends?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.500
Maybe.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.300
Why do you think so?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.750
Tell me why.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.730
They both seem to be having fun.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.770
Did you hear that, Mitsuhide?

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.400
She truly is an interesting girl.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.120
I should take a photo, to show everyone.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.400
They're moving so fast...

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.530
I can't get them in the frame!

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.840
Hey! It's dangerous to 
lean forward that way.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.470
Take this!

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.980
<i>Flame Dragon Fan Strike!</i>

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.200
<i>Lightning Spear Flurry!</i>

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.070
Ow...

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.660
I told you.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.960
My phone!

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.870
It's broken...

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.390
No!

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.960
The screen's black...

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.050
I told you it was dangerous to get too close.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.190
My phone...

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:30.550
What a bothersome girl.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.980
My phone...

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.910
Get up, Hideyoshi.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:40.320
No...

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.450
I'll have mine extra juicy, 
with cream on top...

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.240
I said get up!

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:53.330
We're not here, 
at Kawanaka Island, to sightsee.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.500
We're after the armor those two possess.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.700
But both are equally stubborn.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:06.250
If we ask, neither will simply 
give us the armor.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.840
Indeed.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.850
<i>I refuse.</i>

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:16.400
<i>This Crimson Armor is a sign 
of the Takeda clan's courage.</i>

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.190
<i>I cannot trade it for gold!</i>

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:23.060
<i>Return to Azuchi and 
inform Nobunaga-dono!</i>

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.380
<i>I refuse.</i>

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:30.710
<i>To sell a family treasure, 
bequeathed by my ancestors,</i>

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:32.190
<i>is out of the question!</i>

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:38.420
<i>Tell Nobunaga-dono never to make such 
a foolish request again!</i>

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.790
Fools, obsessed with war.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.130
What to do?

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.780
My lord, I have a plan.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:47.490
Tell me.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:52.010
First, we side with one of them,

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.700
and defeat the other.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.670
Then, we can

00:06:55.670 --> 00:07:00.520
take the armor, as spoils, 
from the one we defeated.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:05.520
And take the armor, 
as a reward, from the victor.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:08.490
I've already prepared everything.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.440
You fool!

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.190
Mitsuhide.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.780
Do you intend to make me

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.080
the laughingstock of the entire land?

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.290
M-My lord, I didn't...

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.400
Idiot!

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.230
Does a warrior resort to such tricks?

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:28.300
No!

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.350
Never!

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:34.660
I cannot interfere in their battle 
for such a scheme.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:37.040
Never suggest that again, understand?

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:37.990
Yes, my lord!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.510
Akerin...

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.670
All my photos and contacts are gone.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.630
You're still bothered by that?

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:02.070
Why don't you just get over it, 
like a woman?

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.350
I can't!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.130
You don't understand

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.500
how important a cell phone is 
to a girl these days, my lord!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:09.840
I do not, no.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.010
You meanie!

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.490
What has you so angry?

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.010
You're like a kid.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.850
I guess I am a kid!

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.230
Hey!

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:35.900
What's wrong, Mitsuhide-san?

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:44.250
Ieyasu-dono, what are you doing here?

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.560
I was passing by, 
on an errand of my own...

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.500
Your eyes are red.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.520
Leave me be.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:57.010
It's my fault anyway.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.790
Yes, you may be right.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.640
H-How did you know...

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.990
Never mind.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:06.980
Did you come here to mock me?

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:07.770
Of course not.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.990
But you're too honest.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.240
Too honest...

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:20.000
You only wish to make 
Nobunaga-san happy, right?

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:26.120
Then why not do something 
that will accomplish that?

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:29.820
Make her happy?

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.810
Thank you, Ieyasu-dono!

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:50.890
<i>You did it, Mitsuhide!</i>

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:54.590
<i>Good girl, good girl.</i>

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.590
<i>Not at all...</i>

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:01.950
<i>I'd do anything to make my lord happy!</i>

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:25.270
<i>I should have, at least, 
run off after eating.</i>

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.140
<i>Why did this happen?</i>

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.210
Stupid dummy!

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:31.920
Stupid dummy lord!

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.360
I'm not helping her find that armor anymore!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.740
What?

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.900
You're all here, right?

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:45.490
Huh?

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.650
Listen!

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:47.690
Akerin?

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.500
You must not let our lord find out about this.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.140
I'm counting on you.

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:53.830
Um...

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.370
H-Hideyoshi!

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.970
What are you doing here?

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.250
What about you, Akerin?

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:01.280
What are you doing here?

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.150
I have no need to tell you.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:06.520
But you're doing something secret here...

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.950
You figured out my secret plan 
to launch a night strike

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:12.200
on Shingen-dono's fortress, 
blaming it on Kenshin-dono;

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.730
then when both

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.160
are even angrier at one another,

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:17.520
to ally with Shingen-dono 
and defeat Kenshin-dono;

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.940
and to finally, 
retrieve both their armor pieces!

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.200
And you hid here

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.910
to get more information, correct?

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.160
I can't look away for a minute!

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:31.540
Um, this is the first I've heard of this...

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.200
You know, it's really easy to get Kenshin

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.780
and Shingen's names mixed up, isn't it?

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:39.630
No, I...

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:44.860
Forget it!

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:45.970
Capture her!

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:48.310
Ma'am!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:53.230
Bye!

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.570
Wait!

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:56.600
Stay still!

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.690
Throw her in the back of the woodshed!

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.180
<i>What's wrong with Akerin?</i>

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:08.740
<i>Our lord just got mad at her.</i>

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:13.190
<i>At this rate, she'll turn into a bad guy!</i>

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:14.420
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.390
That Hideyoshi...

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:19.710
She ran off, without even eating.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:27.250
This is...

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.110
You never ate your dinner,

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.410
and you're certainly 
in a strange position now.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.210
But that aside...

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:51.130
My lord, please stop Akerin!

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.750
Who's there?

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:07.180
My lord!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:13.870
I told you not to interfere 
with Shingen and Kenshin's battle.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.360
Why did you disobey?

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:16.850
W-Well, I...

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.180
Hideyoshi told me everything.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.530
Prepare yourself.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.700
Don't think I'll let you get away with this.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:45.420
Let's finish this today!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.550
Sounds good to me!

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:55.350
Wait!

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:01.360
Nobunaga-dono!

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:04.280
I can't see...

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:08.580
You look so cute, Akerin!

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:10.700
Why, you...

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:15.180
Nobunaga-dono, what are you doing?

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.750
If this concerns the armor, 
I've already refused.

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.750
Yes, it concerns that.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.470
How about it?

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:26.130
Want to have a battle with me 
for the armor?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:27.340
A battle?

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.600
You want me to wager a treasure

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.050
that I received from my ancestors?

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.390
Don't be stupid!

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:35.020
What reason have you to fight us?

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:38.020
I have a reason.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:41.810
Your fights are weak. I can't bear to watch.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.470
A battle with a fixed outcome

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:45.880
is an embarrassment to a warrior.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.320
Fixed?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.640
Take that back.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.390
Our battles are always real...

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.120
Nonsense!

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.700
A war means taking lives.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:00.540
But as you've fought,

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.220
you've begun to take joy in this.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.140
Thus, days and months have passed,

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:09.660
without settling this.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.510
And here is the result!

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:17.880
I'll make you take this seriously!

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:24.520
What a powerful fighting aura...

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.530
You first, Shingen!

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.670
That's Kenshin-san's technique!

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:05.460
Nobunaga, why do you seek the armor?

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:06.940
To conquer the land!

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.940
To conquer?

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:14.200
Why do you wish to conquer?

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:18.330
Then I ask you, Shingen! Kenshin!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.880
Both of you

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:24.190
have been born as generals 
during these wars.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:26.000
Why do you not seek conquest?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.210
Why...

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.630
Why do we not seek conquest?

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:34.640
Why be a warrior, if you do not aim 
for the mountain's summit?

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:37.500
Silence.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:40.310
You have no right 
to speak like that to me, young one!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.790
<i>Flame Dragon Fan Strike!</i>

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:52.480
My lord!      My lord!

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.460
<i>Cruel Blade!</i>

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:19.930
What?

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.290
Shingen!

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.380
I'll give you the armor.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:51.590
But... But not for free.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.340
What?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:57.130
I'm not averse to admitting my defeat.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:02.010
But I refuse to live in shame.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.670
If you want the armor,

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:08.020
then take my head, Nobunaga.

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:11.520
That is my condition.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.610
Understood.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:19.480
W-Wait, my lord!

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:21.330
My lord!

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:27.560
Wait!

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:31.710
Kenshin, what are you doing?

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.990
Move, Kenshin.

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:36.470
If you don't, I will take your head, too.

00:18:37.810 --> 00:18:38.680
Very well.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.220
K-Kenshin.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.800
I beg you, Nobunaga-dono.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:51.810
Take my life and spare Shingen-dono!

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:54.000
Wait, Kenshin!

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.490
You plead for my life?

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.950
What do you think you're doing?

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.630
What else?

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.280
I can't stand

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.410
for you to be defeated 
by anyone but me.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:08.220
Now, Nobunaga-dono.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:10.070
Take my head!

00:19:10.070 --> 00:19:12.210
I'll give you the armor, as well!

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:15.420
Kenshin, you...

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.350
My lord...

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.470
Akerin, what do we do?

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:48.630
Your heads aren't even worth displaying.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.420
All right!

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:16.490
Now I have half the armor!

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.380
Splendid, my lord.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.390
You even saw that Kenshin-dono

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:23.570
would beg for Shingen-dono's life...

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:28.330
I'm overwhelmed by your strategy's depth.

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:30.630
I see!

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.850
That was all part of your plan?

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:34.000
You're amazing!

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:38.300
I wasn't thinking about what 
Kenshin would do at all.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:43.050
I really planned to take Shingen's head.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.430
My lord!

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.630
Mitsuhide!

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:55.020
Don't wash that face off until I tell you.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.880
That's so hilarious!

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.280
I shall not thank you, Kenshin.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:12.230
Nobunaga-dono said it, didn't she?

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:14.210
Take care of your elders.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.510
I just obeyed that rule.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.290
That's terrible.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:22.540
But truly...

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:27.300
Yes, Nobunaga-dono's strength 
is the real thing.

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.560
To conquer, huh?

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:38.770
Now...

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.350
Let us fight...

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:42.610
Fair and square!

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.970
We can't let Nobunaga hold the lead!

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:54.200
<b>Winner: Nobunaga</b>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:52.410
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:31.510
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:31.510
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

